{
  "_doc": [
    "The SFX contract — Design/audio.md §5.1/§5.2 as data. `sfx.py lint` fails on violation;",
    "`sfx.py bake` uses the same numbers as its processing targets.",
    "",
    "maxOnsetMs   — leading silence budget. A UI cue that arrives late reads as input lag.",
    "maxAudibleMs — onset -> last audible sample. THE number that decides mix density (§3.1).",
    "targetPeakDb — bake normalises to this; lint allows +/- peakTolDb. Keeps the set one level.",
    "minCrestDb   — peak-to-RMS. Below this the clip is a compressed drone with no transient and",
    "               will not cut through the board no matter how loud it is (cast_fire = 9.0 dB).",
    "highPassHz   — 2-pole HPF. Removes the low mud that makes small cues sound cheap.",
    "variants     — how many `_1.._n` files the family expects. 0 = single unnumbered file."
  ],

  "defaults": {
    "channels": 1,
    "sampleRate": 44100,
    "maxOnsetMs": 8,
    "targetPeakDb": -6.0,
    "peakTolDb": 1.5,
    "minCrestDb": 10.0,
    "highPassHz": 120,
    "fadeOutMs": 12,
    "releaseMs": 60
  },

  "_endings": [
    "fadeOutMs applies when a clip DECAYED to the threshold on its own — nothing is being removed,",
    "so 12 ms of linear anti-click is all it needs.",
    "releaseMs applies when maxAudibleMs TRUNCATED the clip while it was still loud. It is an",
    "exponential decay and it lives INSIDE the length budget (the clip is cut at maxAudible -",
    "release), so the density arithmetic in audio.md §3 is unaffected.",
    "",
    "Caps are a DENSITY law (§3.1), so they only bind on families that actually overlap: the UI",
    "cues you click repeatedly, and the board impacts running at ~9.6 onsets/s. A once-per-",
    "interaction ceremony (bind, major, error) and a one-per-cast windup (riser_*) have no density",
    "problem at all, and capping them was applying a board law to surfaces that never needed it."
  ],

  "surfaces": {
